      "writtenOn": "2019-05-06T14:28:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sorry, I have not been following the discussion on the bug closely, but are you saying that the compiler replaces accesses to 4 byte values with byte accesses? Is this because of the __packed attribute somewhere?\n\nCould this be addressed by typecasting pointers to non packed uint32_t * when appropriate? It just seems odd and very non portable to use assembler snippets for this.",
